# text = Spare her all the details -- break it to her very tenderly , but tell her that he is dead You have a reason , Walter , for wishing her to know of her husband's death besides the reason you have just mentioned I have A reason connected with that subject which must not be mentioned between us yet ?-- which may never be mentioned to Laura at all I think I understand I think I owe it to her and to you , Walter , to tell her of her husband's death the late Sir Percival Glyde , of Blackwater Park the late Mr . Philip Fairlie , of Limmeridge House plain-looking entrapped the handsomest man in England into marrying her The sins of the fathers shall be visited on the children
